  "problem": "$|-\\frac{8}{7z}|=$",
  "worked_solution": "Firstly, since $|-a|=|a|,$ we can write our expression as\n\n$$\n|\\frac{8}{7z}|.\n$$\n\nThen, we distribute the absolute value over the division, and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\frac{8}{7z}| & = \\\\ \\frac{|8|}{|7z|} & = \\\\ \\frac{8}{|7z|} & = \\\\ \\frac{8}{|7\\cdot z|} & = \\\\ \\frac{8}{|7|\\cdot |z|} & = \\\\ \\frac{8}{7|z|}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
